<title>MOLDOVA: Moldova raises its discount rate to 25 pct annual.</title>
<headline>Moldova raises its discount rate to 25 pct annual.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moldova's National Bank has raised its official discount rate to 25 percent annual from the 21 percent set on February 3, a National Bank official said.</p>
<p>The new rate was set at a credit funds auction on Monday, as six banks acquired a total of 15.64 million lei ($3.35 million) of National Bank reserves.</p>
<p>Today's rate is the highest since July 1995. In 1996 the National Bank kept it discount rate under 22 percent.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
